WEBVTT

00:00:00.309 --> 00:00:02.829
Let me start in a dermatology clinic.

00:00:03.054 --> 00:00:05.975
A patient comes in with a red, scaly rash, and

00:00:05.837 --> 00:00:08.310
six different diseases can look almost identical

00:00:08.172 --> 00:00:11.541
on the skin: psoriasis, seborrheic dermatitis,

00:00:11.639 --> 00:00:15.480
lichen planus, pityriasis rosea, chronic dermatitis

00:00:15.424 --> 00:00:17.449
and pityriasis rubra pilaris.

00:00:17.653 --> 00:00:20.456
Telling them apart matters, because the treatments

00:00:20.318 --> 00:00:20.893
differ.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.890
The data we will use is real: 366 patients from

00:00:24.752 --> 00:00:27.461
a university hospital, published in Artificial

00:00:27.323 --> 00:00:29.831
Intelligence in Medicine in nineteen ninety-eight,

00:00:29.976 --> 00:00:32.838
with 34 findings recorded for each patient and

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.359
the confirmed diagnosis.

00:00:34.542 --> 00:00:36.591
Look at what the table contains.

00:00:36.783 --> 00:00:39.232
Twelve of the findings are clinical, things the

00:00:39.094 --> 00:00:42.192
doctor sees and asks, such as itching, scaling

00:00:42.054 --> 00:00:45.021
and family history, each graded from zero to three.

00:00:45.214 --> 00:00:48.276
Twenty-two come from a biopsy examined under the

00:00:48.139 --> 00:00:49.079
microscope.

00:00:49.304 --> 00:00:52.225
The target column has six possible values, not

00:00:52.087 --> 00:00:55.126
two, and that is exactly the situation softmax

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:55.880
was made for.

00:00:56.108 --> 00:01:00.350
We will train on 293 patients and keep 73 hidden

00:01:00.212 --> 00:01:01.105
for the test.

00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:05.185
So which output layer, and which loss?

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:08.143
If the answer is one of two, a loan going bad or

00:01:08.004 --> 00:01:10.878
not, the sigmoid and the two-class cross-entropy

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.565
from the regression lesson are enough.

00:01:12.792 --> 00:01:15.642
If the answer is one of several, six diagnoses

00:01:15.504 --> 00:01:18.331
or a thousand image classes, you need softmax,

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:20.784
which turns a score per class into a probability

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:23.307
per class, with cross-entropy generalised to many

00:01:23.169 --> 00:01:23.956
classes.

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:26.610
And if the answer is one of fifty thousand, the

00:01:26.471 --> 00:01:28.909
next word a language model should write, it is

00:01:28.771 --> 00:01:31.739
still softmax, just with fifty thousand bars.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.538
The second question is whether the probabilities

00:01:34.399 --> 00:01:35.976
themselves will be used.

00:01:36.203 --> 00:01:38.688
If a doctor or a screening programme acts on the

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:41.354
number, ninety percent must mean ninety percent,

00:01:41.498 --> 00:01:44.242
so calibration has to be checked before deployment.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:47.745
If the inputs are images or free text, a convolutional

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.832
or Transformer network will learn the features,

00:01:49.977 --> 00:01:52.580
but its last layer is this same softmax with this

00:01:52.441 --> 00:01:55.044
same loss, so everything we build here carries

00:01:54.906 --> 00:01:55.965
over unchanged.

00:01:57.446 --> 00:02:00.261
Let us build softmax on three scores small enough

00:02:00.123 --> 00:02:03.504
to do by hand: two, one, and zero point one.

00:02:03.694 --> 00:02:06.002
Step one: raise e to each.

00:02:06.228 --> 00:02:11.142
e to the two is 7.39, e to the one is 2.72, and

00:02:11.004 --> 00:02:13.607
e to the zero point one is 1.11.

00:02:13.811 --> 00:02:16.791
Every bar is now positive, and the gaps between

00:02:16.653 --> 00:02:17.605
them have grown.

00:02:17.792 --> 00:02:21.597
Step two: divide by the total, 11.21.

00:02:21.825 --> 00:02:27.128
The shares are 66 percent, 24 percent, and 10 percent.

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:30.937
They add to one hundred, and the order is preserved.

00:02:31.047 --> 00:02:33.248
That is softmax: exponentiate, then normalise.

00:02:33.417 --> 00:02:36.232
Divide the scores by a temperature first, and you

00:02:36.094 --> 00:02:38.260
control how decisive the model is.

00:02:38.453 --> 00:02:42.565
Cold, at zero point three, the winner takes 96

00:02:42.791 --> 00:02:43.318
percent.

00:02:43.345 --> 00:02:47.740
Hot, at five, the shares flatten to 40, 33 and

00:02:47.956 --> 00:02:48.436
27.

00:02:48.298 --> 00:02:51.112
Same scores, different confidence, and we will

00:02:50.975 --> 00:02:53.247
meet this dial again when we calibrate a model.

00:02:53.458 --> 00:02:56.026
One property every library relies on.

00:02:56.241 --> 00:02:59.387
Add the same constant to all the scores, and softmax

00:02:59.248 --> 00:03:02.040
does not change, because the constant cancels top

00:03:01.901 --> 00:03:02.595
and bottom.

00:03:02.798 --> 00:03:06.050
So before exponentiating, subtract the largest

00:03:05.911 --> 00:03:06.474
score.

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:09.705
Without that, e to the seven hundred and ten overflows

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:12.489
a computer's number format; with it, the biggest

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:14.021
exponent is always zero.

00:03:14.208 --> 00:03:17.247
And with just two classes, softmax collapses to

00:03:17.109 --> 00:03:19.936
a function you have met: the sigmoid of the difference

00:03:19.798 --> 00:03:20.903
of the two scores.

00:03:21.107 --> 00:03:24.193
Logistic regression is softmax with two bars.

00:03:25.654 --> 00:03:26.712
Now the loss.

00:03:26.936 --> 00:03:29.681
The surprise of an event with probability p is

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:30.801
minus the log of p.

00:03:30.663 --> 00:03:32.499
Certain, zero surprise.

00:03:32.726 --> 00:03:35.565
A coin flip, 0.693.

00:03:35.792 --> 00:03:38.207
A one-in-ten event, 2.3.

00:03:38.401 --> 00:03:40.945
Cross-entropy charges the model the surprise of

00:03:40.806 --> 00:03:43.857
the true answer, and nothing else: minus the log

00:03:43.719 --> 00:03:45.839
of the probability it gave to the truth.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.334
Our model said 66 percent for the first class,

00:03:49.196 --> 00:03:51.138
and that class is the truth.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:56.633
The loss is minus the log of 0.659, which is 0.417.

00:03:56.495 --> 00:03:58.957
Had it said ten percent, the loss would have been

00:03:58.818 --> 00:04:02.082
two point three; had it said ninety-nine, almost

00:04:02.276 --> 00:04:03.122
nothing.

00:04:02.983 --> 00:04:05.208
Confident and right is cheap.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:06.517
Confident and wrong is ruinous.

00:04:06.708 --> 00:04:09.028
The name comes from information theory.

00:04:09.222 --> 00:04:12.131
Cross-entropy equals the entropy of the truth plus

00:04:11.993 --> 00:04:14.361
the Kullback-Leibler divergence from the truth

00:04:14.222 --> 00:04:15.221
to the prediction.

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:18.167
For a single correct label the entropy is zero,

00:04:18.288 --> 00:04:21.104
so minimising cross-entropy is exactly minimising

00:04:20.965 --> 00:04:23.521
the divergence: making the prediction match the

00:04:23.383 --> 00:04:24.005
truth.

00:04:25.488 --> 00:04:28.114
Here is the reason these two are always paired.

00:04:28.315 --> 00:04:31.201
Differentiate the loss with respect to the scores.

00:04:31.428 --> 00:04:34.113
The derivative of softmax is messy on its own,

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:36.932
p i times delta i j minus p j.

00:04:37.126 --> 00:04:39.788
But push it through minus the log, and everything

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:40.507
cancels.

00:04:40.733 --> 00:04:44.372
The gradient is p minus y: prediction minus truth.

00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:49.603
With our numbers: the prediction is 0.659, 0.242,

00:04:49.736 --> 00:04:53.720
0.099; the truth is one, zero, zero.

00:04:53.934 --> 00:05:00.488
So the gradient is -0.341, 0.242, 0.099.

00:05:00.681 --> 00:05:03.390
Push the true class's score up, push the others

00:05:03.252 --> 00:05:06.327
down, each by exactly how much it was over-believed.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.902
Take four gradient steps on the scores and the

00:05:08.764 --> 00:05:12.840
true class's share rises to 0.885; the loss falls

00:05:12.703 --> 00:05:16.002
from 0.417 to 0.122.

00:05:16.227 --> 00:05:18.865
This is the line where backpropagation begins in

00:05:18.727 --> 00:05:21.613
every classifier: the error signal at the output

00:05:21.474 --> 00:05:23.145
is simply p minus y.

00:05:24.613 --> 00:05:25.871
Now the real job.

00:05:26.096 --> 00:05:29.146
We standardise the 34 findings, give each of the

00:05:29.008 --> 00:05:31.705
six diseases its own row of weights, and train

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:34.359
by gradient descent on exactly the loss and gradient

00:05:34.221 --> 00:05:35.290
we just derived.

00:05:35.518 --> 00:05:37.943
The mean cross-entropy on the training patients

00:05:37.806 --> 00:05:41.528
falls from 1.792, which is the log of six, the

00:05:41.391 --> 00:05:44.170
loss of pure guessing, to 0.02.

00:05:44.333 --> 00:05:45.345
Did it work?

00:05:45.538 --> 00:05:48.471
On the 73 patients the model has never seen it

00:05:48.333 --> 00:05:52.846
is right 71 times, 97 percent, and the correct

00:05:52.708 --> 00:05:54.754
diagnosis is always in its top two.

00:05:54.616 --> 00:05:58.139
The original authors reported about 96.2 percent

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.368
with their own method in nineteen ninety-eight,

00:06:00.229 --> 00:06:02.868
so a softmax regression with the right loss is

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:04.884
already at the published standard.

00:06:04.746 --> 00:06:07.455
The confusion matrix shows where the few mistakes

00:06:07.316 --> 00:06:10.214
fall, and even the rarest disease, with only 20

00:06:10.076 --> 00:06:11.937
patients in the whole set, is recognised.

00:06:12.125 --> 00:06:15.153
Here is one real patient from the test set, aged

00:06:15.014 --> 00:06:15.919
48.

00:06:16.146 --> 00:06:19.303
The model gives 53 percent to chronic dermatitis

00:06:19.165 --> 00:06:23.159
and 46 percent to pityriasis rosea, a close call,

00:06:23.021 --> 00:06:26.461
and the confirmed diagnosis is chronic dermatitis.

00:06:26.323 --> 00:06:29.798
That is the readout a clinician wants: not a single

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:32.546
label, but the probabilities, so that a near tie

00:06:32.408 --> 00:06:34.198
is visible and a second test can be ordered.

00:06:35.666 --> 00:06:38.316
At enterprise scale the same layer sits at the

00:06:38.177 --> 00:06:39.884
end of much bigger networks.

00:06:40.085 --> 00:06:42.488
Google's lung-cancer screening model, published

00:06:42.349 --> 00:06:44.928
in Nature Medicine in twenty nineteen, reads a

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:45.742
chest C.T.

00:06:45.604 --> 00:06:47.983
with a three-dimensional convolutional network

00:06:47.844 --> 00:06:50.318
and ends in a softmax over two outcomes.

00:06:50.545 --> 00:06:54.045
It reached an area under the curve of 94.4 percent

00:06:53.906 --> 00:06:57.936
on 6,716 scans from the National Lung Screening

00:06:58.092 --> 00:07:01.026
Trial, and without a prior scan it made 11 percent

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:03.950
fewer false positives and 5 percent fewer false

00:07:03.811 --> 00:07:06.367
negatives than six radiologists.

00:07:06.229 --> 00:07:08.619
The probability from that softmax sets who is called

00:07:08.021 --> 00:07:08.619
back.

00:07:08.833 --> 00:07:12.250
And a language model is a classifier over its vocabulary.

00:07:12.444 --> 00:07:17.771
GPT-two ends in a softmax over 50,257 tokens, trained

00:07:17.632 --> 00:07:20.636
by cross-entropy on the next word; e to that loss

00:07:20.498 --> 00:07:23.006
is the perplexity quoted in every model report,

00:07:23.139 --> 00:07:25.188
and a temperature divides the scores before the

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:27.818
softmax to make the model more or less decisive.

00:07:28.019 --> 00:07:30.658
Same formula, fifty thousand bars.

00:07:32.154 --> 00:07:33.814
Now, when it fails.

00:07:34.026 --> 00:07:36.039
First, over-confidence.

00:07:36.233 --> 00:07:38.765
Train the same model for much longer without any

00:07:38.627 --> 00:07:41.336
regularisation and its average confidence creeps

00:07:41.198 --> 00:07:45.334
up to 98.7 percent while its accuracy slips to

00:07:45.502 --> 00:07:49.166
96 percent; the calibration error more than doubles,

00:07:49.028 --> 00:07:51.700
from 0.018 to 0.041.

00:07:51.561 --> 00:07:54.070
Large deep networks do this far more severely,

00:07:53.932 --> 00:07:56.676
which is why temperature scaling, a single number

00:07:56.538 --> 00:07:59.199
dividing the scores, is fitted on held-out data

00:07:59.061 --> 00:08:00.650
before a medical model is deployed.

00:08:00.833 --> 00:08:03.377
Second, the inputs you will not have.

00:08:03.571 --> 00:08:06.387
Train on the twelve clinical findings alone, as

00:08:06.248 --> 00:08:09.228
in a clinic that cannot do a biopsy, and accuracy

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:12.009
falls from 97 to 92 percent.

00:08:11.871 --> 00:08:14.486
A model is only as good as the inputs available

00:08:14.347 --> 00:08:17.139
at the moment of the decision, so check which columns

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.624
will actually exist in production.

00:08:18.833 --> 00:08:20.599
Third, label noise.

00:08:20.814 --> 00:08:23.441
Flip twenty percent of the training diagnoses at

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:25.906
random, the kind of error that creeps into real

00:08:25.767 --> 00:08:28.971
records, and the test accuracy drops from 97 to

00:08:28.833 --> 00:08:31.191
86 percent.

00:08:31.052 --> 00:08:33.455
Cross-entropy trusts every label completely, so

00:08:33.316 --> 00:08:35.919
the quality of the labels is the ceiling on the

00:08:35.321 --> 00:08:35.919
model.

00:08:36.083 --> 00:08:38.038
Fourth, the hidden second.

00:08:38.265 --> 00:08:40.974
The top label hides how close the race was.

00:08:41.201 --> 00:08:44.406
In our small test set one patient had two diseases

00:08:44.267 --> 00:08:46.752
within a few points of each other, and in a large

00:08:46.614 --> 00:08:48.356
deployment that will be hundreds.

00:08:48.571 --> 00:08:51.787
Report the probabilities, flag the near ties, and

00:08:51.649 --> 00:08:52.849
let a person look.

00:08:54.321 --> 00:08:56.145
So here is the checklist.

00:08:56.337 --> 00:09:00.602
Two answers, sigmoid; several, softmax; thousands,

00:09:00.676 --> 00:09:01.876
still softmax.

00:09:02.077 --> 00:09:05.128
Subtract the maximum before exponentiating.

00:09:05.332 --> 00:09:08.454
Train with cross-entropy, whose gradient is prediction

00:09:08.316 --> 00:09:09.373
minus truth.

00:09:09.568 --> 00:09:12.076
Judge the model on patients it has never seen,

00:09:12.186 --> 00:09:15.166
with accuracy, the confusion matrix and the top-two

00:09:15.028 --> 00:09:15.603
rate.

00:09:15.792 --> 00:09:18.807
Then check the four failures: calibrate the confidence

00:09:18.669 --> 00:09:21.484
on held-out data, train only on inputs that will

00:09:21.346 --> 00:09:24.550
exist at decision time, audit the labels, and report

00:09:24.412 --> 00:09:26.649
the probabilities rather than a single label.

00:09:26.843 --> 00:09:29.976
Do that, and you have built what a diagnostic model

00:09:29.838 --> 00:09:31.710
and a language model both end with.

00:09:31.912 --> 00:09:35.010
Next: linear and logistic regression, where we

00:09:34.872 --> 00:09:36.767
trace this neuron to its root.
